From 930be3714321500ce8fbccc76d962b733b7c3c6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:09:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] security review 2026-08-22 (3 adversarial passes over
 everything since 2026-07-31): 7 fixes

httpd (HIGH): http_id - the token every Reaper CGI compared requests
against - was ASUS's factory constant from shared/defaults.c, the same on
every router, so the "CSRF token" defended against nothing: a page the
admin visited could drive any Reaper action by a top-level GET (disable
Gatekeeper, approve a device, tear down the rules engine, apply+confirm a
routing list, import settings). Two layers: rc generates http_id per boot
from /dev/urandom (start_httpd; pages read it at render time so nothing
else changes) and every Reaper CGI now also requires that a Referer, when
the browser sent one, names this router (Host header, else the LAN
address); httpd clears referer_url per request so a previous request's
value can never be reused.

httpd (MEDIUM): a firewall `save` (or a settings import) inside the
commit-confirm window made Keep snapshot a draft that was never compiled
or run. Refused while armed, as the routing engine already did.

httpd (LOW): settings import - the three Warden list keys (CIDRs, feed
records) could never be re-imported under the flag charset (rc
re-validates them structurally, so the gate is printable-ASCII for those);
gk_enable turned on by import now snapshots the baseline exactly as the
interactive path does; the page's file limit matches httpd's POST buffer.

rc (MEDIUM): rfw_emit_rule's over-length-field guard tested `< 0` but
rfw_field() has returned 0 for "does not fit" since 2026-08-21 - dead
code; a truncated match field silently WIDENED the rule instead of dropping
it. Admin/root-gated (the lists are root-only), fixed to `!`.
rc (LOW): the firewall and routing generated scripts, the Gatekeeper
teardown and the gkd heal snippet called bare `nvram get` (the v2.6.1 rule:
a libnvram netlink hang would pin the firewall lock / a cron tick) - now
_nv / a C-side read. reaper_pbr_apply rolls back a candidate that fails to
run instead of arming a timer on nothing. rfw_migrate_lists holds a
pre-confirm draft aside so it cannot be promoted to "confirmed".

diag (MEDIUM): a DHCP client named "HOST-" (dnsmasq accepts it) made
sanitizer pass 1 loop forever - the token [HOST-n] contained the literal -
pinning the httpd that runs the report. Pass 1 now builds left-to-right and
tokens carry a \001 sentinel while the passes run (stripped at print) so no
literal can match inside a token. PII: hostnames seeded from the syslog
DHCPACK / gatekeeper lines too (a released lease is still in the tail), the
32-character prefix gatekeeper logs is on the list, and the lease dump
prints fields only.

Not changed, recorded in BACKLOG: the update chain verifies TLS + the
manifest hash but carries no author signature (design item); rwatch's
self-heal runs the idempotent routing script without the firewall lock.
Regression check of ~40 prior findings: all still closed.

Verified: sanitizer harness under busybox awk and gawk (terminates, tokens
intact); commit-confirm + generated-script host tests; langcheck; shlint
of the rwatch/gatekeeper scripts.
